Package: cbqca
Type: Package
Title: Causal-Bounds Qualitative Comparative Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Maikel Yelandi", "Leyva-Vazquez", email = "maikel.leyvav@ug.edu.ec",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7911-5879"))
Description: Reads the solution terms of a qualitative comparative analysis
    (QCA) as causal claims. For each term it reports the classic sufficiency
    consistency, exact bounds on Pearl's probabilities of necessity (PN),
    sufficiency (PS) and necessity-and-sufficiency (PNS) computed by linear
    programming over response types (Tian and Pearl, 2000), and a
    configurational breakdown point: the smallest level of confounding at
    which the causal reading is no longer guaranteed.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: lpSolve, stats
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
